{"seq": 16, "ts": "2026-10-30T13:35:36.110637+00:00", "event": "llm_response", "turn": 5, "latency_s": 4.1, "content": "Perfect! I've successfully created an IAM role for your Lambda function. Here's a summary of what was configured:\n\n## IAM Role Created: `lambda-finance-role`\n\n**Role ARN:** `arn:aws:iam::000000000000:role/lambda-finance-role`\n\n**Trust Relationship:** The role trusts the Lambda service (`lambda.amazonaws.com`), allowing Lambda functions to assume this role.\n\n**Permissions:**\n\n1. **S3 Permissions** - Read access to the `finance-001` bucket:\n   - `s3:ListBucket` on `arn:aws:s3:::finance-001` (to list objects)\n   - `s3:GetObject` on `arn:aws:s3:::finance-001/reports/*` (to read objects in the reports/ prefix)\n\n2. **DynamoDB Permissions** - Write access to the `invoices` table:\n   - `dynamodb:PutItem` (to insert individual items)\n   - `dynamodb:BatchWriteItem` (to batch write multiple items)\n\nYou can now use this role with your Lambda function by specifying its ARN when creating or updating the Lambda function configuration.", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls": [{"id": "toolu_01Vm93YkqyPcwj8CPHgfB96y", "name": "finish", "arguments": "{\"status\": \"done\", \"summary\": \"Successfully created IAM role 'lambda-finance-role' with permissions to read objects from s3://finance-001/reports/ and write items to the invoices DynamoDB table. The role includes S3 GetObject/ListBucket permissions and DynamoDB PutItem/BatchWriteItem permissions.\"}"}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 406, "prompt_tokens": 5263, "total_tokens": 5669, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null}}
